From 00eef6af42d57b7da186b85deba61d3805c16967 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 06:26:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 234/638] build: enter the AROS POSIX startup [chromium] [aros]

AI_PHASE: chromium-phase-4-browser-link

AI_STATUS: done

ROOT_CAUSE: The AROS link used startup.o rather than nixmain.o, so posixc path translation and process-local environment initialization were absent before ChromiumMain.

FIX_REASON: Select the AROS POSIX-aware startup at link time with -nix. Chromium has no __NIX__ source branches, so no broad recompilation contract is introduced.

SCOPE: build/toolchain/aros/BUILD.gn

VALIDATION: Regenerated the chrome link command and confirmed x86_64-aros-g++ receives -nix; rebuilt //chrome/browser:browser archive.

RISK: All AROS Chromium executables from this toolchain now enter through nixmain; native AROS paths must be passed through posixc-compatible forms.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap;
---
 build/toolchain/aros/BUILD.gn | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/build/toolchain/aros/BUILD.gn b/build/toolchain/aros/BUILD.gn
index dc4e6c0a7e..9f516313f7 100644
--- a/build/toolchain/aros/BUILD.gn
+++ b/build/toolchain/aros/BUILD.gn
@@ -29,7 +29,9 @@ gcc_toolchain("x64") {
   extra_cppflags =
       "-m64 -mcmodel=large -mno-red-zone -mno-ms-bitfields" +
       " -fno-asynchronous-unwind-tables -fno-omit-frame-pointer" + _sysroot_flag
-  extra_ldflags = "-m64 -mcmodel=large" + _sysroot_flag
+  # Select AROS's POSIX-aware startup, which initializes posixc path and
+  # process-local environment semantics before ChromiumMain runs.
+  extra_ldflags = "-m64 -mcmodel=large -nix" + _sysroot_flag
 
   toolchain_args = {
     current_cpu = "x64"
